  "title": "KB NDE 4275",
  "date": "Summer of 1968",
  "content": "I was swimming in the river, under the watch of my older sister. We were not supposed to be there without an adult but I went along with my sister and her friends. I was bouncing around in the river. I was not a good swimmer, I think I could float and doggy paddle. The river bottom changes constantly, so in playing on what had previously been a sandbar, I stepped off and was over my head in water. I struggled to gain my footing but began to sink. Eventually I stopped struggling and a feeling of calm came over me. I saw my life (as brief as it was) flash before me. I experienced feeling very peaceful, and happy to go toward the bright light ahead. The next thing I recall was someone grabbing me. My sister says she looked over and saw my hair floating on top of the water (my hair was waist length at the time). She rushed over and pulled me out by it. I do not recall anything that happened next. This experience was something we did not talk about because we were afraid we would get in trouble for being where we should not have been. Only many years later did it come up.",
